&lt;h3&gt;🧡 About Alma&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Alma, we believe sustainable commerce depends on fair, well-balanced trade. Because finance plays a pivotal role in business, our mission is to put it back in its rightful place, serving merchants and consumers.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our installment and deferred payment solutions help merchants boost sales by 20% or more, increase customer loyalty, and deliver a seamless shopping experience, without encouraging bad debt.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As the buy now pay later leader in France and active in 10 European countries, we&#39;ve empowered more than 25,000 merchants and 10 million consumers.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;With 380+ Almakers and €100M+ ARR, Alma is scaling rapidly across Europe as a member of the Next40, and we&#39;re just getting started!&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;👐 About the team&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Revenue at Alma covers the entire customer lifecycle, from lead generation to churn. It brings together Marketing, Partnerships, Sales and Account Management, representing more than 100 talented professionals.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Revenue Operations plays a key role in helping these teams work together around shared goals, reliable data and efficient processes. The team supports Revenue leaders in improving performance, making better decisions and scaling the organisation.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This position is a permanent contract, based in Paris, with 2 days of remote work per week.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will report to &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.linkedin.com/in/basil-lizotte-aa155182&quot;&gt;Basil Lizotte&lt;/a&gt;, and work closely with Revenue teams, the Central Data Team, Ops &amp;amp; Risk, Product and Tech.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;💼 About the job&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As Senior Business Analyst, Revenue Operations, you will create strategic insights that help Alma&#39;s Revenue teams understand their performance, identify growth opportunities and improve their speed and efficiency.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will work at the intersection of data, business and strategy, turning complex questions into clear recommendations and practical tools.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;Build reliable data foundations for Revenue&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and evolve business-facing data models by combining relevant CRM, revenue and operational data sources.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Improve and maintain existing models and contribute to reliable end-to-end data pipelines.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;Turn business questions into strategic insights&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Analyse Alma&#39;s target markets, market share, market dynamics and the key drivers behind commercial wins.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design ad hoc tools and models to help Revenue teams answer tactical business questions and make faster decisions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;Improve performance monitoring and revenue growth&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and manage dashboards, KPIs and revenue forecasts so teams and leadership can monitor business health and progress against their goals.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support Revenue leaders in setting the right targets, understanding growth dynamics and prioritising their roadmap.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;Drive data excellence across Revenue&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Promote data-informed ways of working across Marketing, Partnerships, Sales and Account Management.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate closely with the Central Data Team to maintain high standards of data quality and consistency across the organisation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;🧰 You will work with&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;SQL, Looker, LookML, Claude Code, Python, dbt, BigQuery, GCP, Rudderstack, Segment, Salesforce&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;🧩 About you&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;To succeed in this job&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have strong SQL skills and are comfortable working with large datasets, raw CRM data and revenue-related information, including Salesforce data.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have experience building business-facing data models, dashboards, forecasts or performance analyses from the initial question through to clear recommendations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You can define relevant KPIs, assess business impact and communicate complex analysis in a clear and actionable way to different stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have approximately 4 to 7 years of experience in data analysis, business analysis or a similar role, ideally in a fast-growing technology or fintech environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;And it will be nice if you also&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have experience with Looker and LookML.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You are comfortable with Python and modern data tools such as dbt, BigQuery or GCP.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have worked with tracking tools such as Rudderstack or Segment, as well as experimentation methodologies such as A/B testing, significance testing and causal analysis.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You are curious about AI-assisted tools and are interested in using tools such as Claude Code in your daily workflow.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Don&#39;t meet every single requirement? At Alma, we believe great hires come from diverse paths. If this role excites you, we encourage you to apply. We value potential, curiosity and the ability to grow as much as experience.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;🧘 Your Alma experience&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;The culture&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Alma, collective intelligence is at the heart of the way we work. We are building an international company in a fast-growing environment, where people are encouraged to take ownership, share ideas and learn from one another.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will have access to our Learning &amp;amp; Development Platform, regular feedback and opportunities to develop your expertise and career path. As Alma continues to grow across Europe, you will have the opportunity to work with colleagues from different teams, countries and areas of expertise.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are committed to building a fair and inclusive workplace. We monitor our gender equality index and remain committed to pay equity, transparency and equal opportunities across the organisation.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;The role itself&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If you join Alma, you will be able to grow and have an impact by:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Influencing strategic decisions across the full Revenue organisation, from lead generation to churn.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Combining analytical depth, business understanding and direct exposure to senior stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Helping Revenue teams build a stronger data culture and create more efficient ways of working as Alma scales across Europe.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;🤑 Compensation &amp;amp; benefits&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Competitive salary&lt;/strong&gt; based on 12 months&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Profit-sharing and employee savings plan&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Health insurance&lt;/strong&gt;: &lt;strong&gt;100%&lt;/strong&gt; covered by Alma, including family package&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Disability insurance&lt;/strong&gt;: &lt;strong&gt;100%&lt;/strong&gt; covered by Alma&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Sport&lt;/strong&gt;: partnerships with &lt;strong&gt;Gymlib&lt;/strong&gt; and &lt;strong&gt;ClassPass&lt;/strong&gt;, or &lt;strong&gt;€30/month&lt;/strong&gt; reimbursement for your sports activities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Maternity/paternity leave&lt;/strong&gt;: salary maintained at 100% during leave, with no seniority requirement. Return to work at a 4/5 schedule paid at 100% for 8 weeks&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Sustainable Mobility Package (FMD)&lt;/strong&gt;: &lt;strong&gt;€544.80/year&lt;/strong&gt;, excluding full-remote contracts&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Meal vouchers&lt;/strong&gt;: &lt;strong&gt;€10/day&lt;/strong&gt;, 50% covered by Alma&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Mental health&lt;/strong&gt;: free access to the MindDay platform&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Paid time off&lt;/strong&gt;: 25 days per year, plus additional paid leave granted to employees on executive contracts&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Access to our &lt;strong&gt;Learning &amp;amp; Development Platform&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;2 weeks of full remote work possible per year&lt;/strong&gt; during the summer&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;🎯 Interview process&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Video screen with Lydia a Talent Acquisition team member&lt;/strong&gt; to discuss your background, motivation and the role.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Experience interview with Basil Lizotte or/and Gaspard Zha&lt;/strong&gt;, lasting 45 minutes, to discuss the role, the team and your experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Home assignment and case study&lt;/strong&gt;, lasting 1 hour, with members team.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;On-site team fit interview&lt;/strong&gt;, lasting 30 minutes.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;On-site N+2 interview&lt;/strong&gt; with Antoine de la Rivière, lasting 30 minutes.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Reference check&lt;/strong&gt; with at least two professional references.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;🌍 Diversity &amp;amp; Inclusion&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Alma, we believe that diversity fuels innovation and makes our community stronger. We are committed to building a workplace where every person feels seen, respected, and empowered to do their best work, whatever their gender, background, ethnicity, age, sexual orientation, religion, disability or lived experience.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As an equal opportunity employer, we welcome applicants from all walks of life, and all employment decisions are made based on qualifications, merit and business needs.&lt;/p&gt;<p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.fr/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in France</a> on Arbeitnow</a>

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Brief info about Vinted&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p data-renderer-start-pos=&quot;1&quot;&gt;&lt;span data-sheets-root=&quot;1&quot;&gt;Our mission is to make second-hand the first choice, and we&#39;re looking for people who want to help us get there. Every day, we work together to help our members buy and sell pre-loved clothing and lifestyle items, giving each piece a second life – or even a third. &lt;br&gt;The Vinted Group is made up of three business units that support this mission:&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://careers.vinted.com/marketplace&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;Vinted Marketplace&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/strong&gt; is Europe’s leading platform for second-hand fashion and a go-to destination for all kinds of pre-loved items, with a growing range of categories. Our platform connects millions of members across 20+ markets, helping great items find a new life.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://careers.vinted.com/vintedgo&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Vinted Go&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/a&gt; enhances the shipping experience with a vast network of over 500,000 pick-up and drop-off points, partnering with more than 60 carriers across Europe, with added services like item verification for peace of mind on high-value pieces.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://careers.vinted.com/vintedpay&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Vinted Pay&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/a&gt; is the newest part of the Vinted Group, dedicated to bringing secure, reliable payments to buyers and sellers across Europe. Seamlessly integrated into the Vinted app, it helps keep every transaction safe, efficient, and easy for our members.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Founded in 2008 in Lithuania, Vinted began as a way for friends to find new homes for clothes they no longer needed. In 2019, we became Lithuania&#39;s first unicorn! Today, our headquarters remain in Vilnius, and we&#39;ve grown with offices across Europe, supported by a team of over 2,000 people.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Missions and activities of the position&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;1. Project phase – owner&#39;s engineer for Maintenance&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Represent Maintenance in every phase of new equipment projects (starting with the MRS1 cross-belt sorter), from design reviews to FAT, SAT, commissioning and ramp-up. For the sorter, whose design is already set, take over the installed system and optimise it after go-live.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work side by side with the OEM / integrator engineers: collect technical knowledge, challenge design choices, maintainability, access, spare-part strategy and the proposed maintenance plan before they are frozen.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define and verify the Maintenance acceptance criteria (documentation, training, spare parts, safety, availability targets). The Maintenance sign-off is mandatory: no handover to operations without it.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Track and drive to closure the technical punch list and warranty issues raised during commissioning and the warranty period.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;2. Technical file &amp;amp; spare parts&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and own the equipment technical file: as-built electrical and mechanical drawings, PLC and software versions, parameter backups, network architecture, safety documentation, OEM manuals.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Create the asset hierarchy and criticality analysis in the CMMS.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define the critical spare-parts list (references, min/max stock, lead times) and keep it up to date.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Reduce dependency on the OEM: identify and qualify second-source suppliers for critical parts, run compatibility tests and document equivalences.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Propose spare-parts and supplier decisions to the Maintenance Manager; after an initial period, take these decisions autonomously within agreed limits, with the Maintenance Manager&#39;s validation.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;3. Maintenance strategy &amp;amp; procedures&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Write and maintain preventive maintenance plans, corrective procedures and troubleshooting guides for the equipment family, based on OEM data, FMEA and field experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Monitor equipment performance (availability, MTBF, MTTR, top failure modes), lead root-cause analysis on recurring or major failures and implement permanent corrective actions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Challenge the original design when needed and drive engineering changes: retrofits, drive and firmware updates, software or parameter optimisation, with the OEM and internal stakeholders.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;4. Training &amp;amp; technical support&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Train the operational maintenance team (technicians and operatives) on the equipment, its software/HMI and the troubleshooting procedures; validate their autonomy level.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Act as the level-2 / level-3 technical expert for the equipment family on site and remotely, across sites.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;5. Escalation, vendor &amp;amp; SLA management&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own technical escalations through to resolution: with the Tetris team (Vinted&#39;s internal tools and sorting logic) when the issue is on the software or data side, and with OEM / integrator support (SAV) when it is on the equipment side.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead the diagnosis that tells which side an issue comes from (equipment, controls, Vinted software), with facts and data.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work within the after-sales and maintenance agreements already in place with OEMs: make the most of them day to day, monitor performance against SLAs and warranty terms, feed lessons learned into future renewals, and provide the technical evidence to the program managers, who own the contractual relationship.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prepare and lead technical review meetings with OEMs and integrators.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;6. Safety &amp;amp; compliance&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure the equipment and its maintenance comply with machine safety requirements (CE marking, safety functions, lock-out/tag-out) and site H&amp;amp;S standards.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support safety audits and regulatory inspections, and drive the resulting corrective actions to completion.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Occasional responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Take ownership of additional equipment families (e.g. conveyors, AMR fleets, Monk lines) once the cross-belt is stable.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support pre-project technical due diligence on new equipment (specifications, vendor benchmarks, maintainability review).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Participate in the hiring and onboarding of maintenance technicians and future engineers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Interests, constraints, difficulties of the position&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;High-visibility role on new strategic automation investments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Site-based in an operational warehouse, with regular presence on the shop floor.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Regular travel to MRS1, OEM premises (FAT) and other Vinted Go sites, especially during commissioning.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Day-based role, no on-call. Flexibility needed during commissioning, ramp-up and major incidents (possible early, late or weekend work).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Needs to influence without authority: OEMs, integrators, IT and program management teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Your profile&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Knowledge &amp;amp; experience&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Engineering degree (Master&#39;s / Bac+5) in automation, electrical, mechatronics or industrial engineering, or Bac+2/3 with equivalent proven experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;At least 3 years&#39; experience, ideally 5 or more, as Equipment Engineer, Automation Engineer, Tool Owner or Maintenance/Reliability Engineer in a highly automated environment: parcel sortation and intralogistics, airport baggage handling, logistics or other automated industries.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Automation background required.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven involvement in at least one industrial equipment project from FAT/SAT to ramp-up, working with OEMs or integrators.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Technical skills&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Able to read and diagnose complete PLC and HMI programs (Siemens TIA Portal and/or Rockwell, Beckhoff) and to make controlled modifications; industrial networks (Profinet, Profibus, EtherCAT, Ethernet/IP).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drives (parameters, firmware), servo motors, sensors, scanners / DWS, pneumatics; reading electrical and mechanical schematics.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Retrofit experience and component qualification (equivalence, compatibility testing)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Safety PLCs and machine safety functions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Understanding of the interfaces between equipment controls, SCADA/WCS and IT systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Reliability methods: FMEA, RCA (5 Why, Ishikawa, 8D), criticality analysis; CMMS and PM planning.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Sortation equipment experience (cross-belt, tilt-tray, shoe sorters) is a strong plus.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;French electrical certification (habilitation électrique BR / B2V / BC) or ability to obtain it.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fluent French and professional English (OEMs and the Vinted Go network work in English).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Behavioural skills&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong ownership: treats the equipment as their own, from design to end of life.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Able to challenge OEM and integrator engineers constructively, with facts and data.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Structured and disciplined in documentation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Good teacher: enjoys transferring knowledge to technicians.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Calm and solution-oriented under production pressure; strong safety mindset.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;br&gt;Please note: the main tasks and skills identified and noted in the function described above may need to evolve depending on the constraints and organisation specific to the company and its environment. They are, therefore, indicative and not contractual.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;Working at Vinted&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Individual learning budget&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Each year, you’ll be given a learning budget (starting at €3,000), and a total of up to 10 working days over a 2-year period to support your personal and professional development.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Equal opportunity&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We welcome applications from everybody, regardless of your background, identity, or life experiences. Job openings come with guides, not checklists. If you’re excited about a role, but don’t identify with every point in the ‘About you’ section, apply anyway – you might still be the perfect match!&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-pay-transparency&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;The annual gross salary range for this position is:&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;€45.000&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;€60.000 EUR&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;<p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.fr">Jobs in France</a> on Arbeitnow</a>

&lt;p&gt;As a Production Engineer, you will play a key role within our Test Engineering team, programming test software and documenting test procedures to scale production of our next-generation drone platforms. In this position, you will take ownership of verification and production test equipment, from defining test concepts to designing automated test solutions, jigs and needle-bed adapters that help us improve yield and reliability. You’ll collaborate closely with our software and electronics engineers and OEM partners to enhance test coverage and reduce testing time, driving efficiency across our manufacturing process.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a hands-on role in a fast-paced, agile environment, offering the opportunity to design creative, practical test solutions from concept through to mass production. This involves balancing the transition from our existing test setups to more scalable and complete solutions in a pragmatic and iterative way for a number of different projects.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Beyond test engineering, you’ll apply your software expertise across the broader hardware and software team by supporting the engineering validation efforts of new products. You will also visit OEMs to support new product integrations and support small scale engineering runs in person.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities and Duties&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Research, design and build test solutions, including auto generated, 3D printed test equipment and CNC milled custom test jigs, and needle-bed adapters to enable low-volume prototyping and mid- to high-volume PCB production.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Plan and execute product verification, covering test case definition, execution, analysis, and comprehensive documentation, also for repair guidance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Write Python code and STM32 firmware to test our embedded products from the inside (selftest) and outside (via test fixture).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with cross-functional engineering teams by offering technical guidance and hands-on support for testing and validation of advanced avionics PCBs and modular systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Specify and document additional manufacturer tests (like flying probe) to allow for a layered, holistic approach to test coverage.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Write Repair Guides that document the error cases and the affected components.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Guide manufacturers with new product integrations usually in person in the factory.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage tracking systems across multiple locations to inspect the product workflow.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support internal CI systems with real hardware to validate test procedures before upgrading test fixtures at OEMs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Qualifications and Skills&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor&#39;s or Master&#39;s degree in Electrical Engineering, Computer Science or a related technical field.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficiency in modern Python and C/C++ also applied to embedded systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of experience in programming software that runs on real hardware and testing it on real hardware.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;CAD experience (e.g., Onshape) and soldering skills are required.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Practical experience in Linux, microcontroller programming, 3D printing, and related prototyping tools.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Pragmatic, solution-oriented mindset.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Good verbal and written English communication skills.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Benefits&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Flexible working hours&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Stock Options&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Generous holiday allowance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Company pension plan&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Car parking&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Enhanced maternity &amp;amp; paternity leave&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Mental health and wellbeing support&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Learning and development opportunities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Auterion&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are building the leading software and electronics platform for AI-powered autonomous systems for enterprise and government customers. Our team is supporting the most important missions and solving the most challenging problems.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Auterion, we bring together the sharpest minds who love to solve the hardest problems. Join a vibrant team built on innovation, openness, and excellence, where you’ll be empowered to develop ideas, collaborate across all levels, and make an impact that matters.&lt;/p&gt;<p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.ch/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in Switzerland</a> on Arbeitnow</a>

&lt;p&gt;We are looking for an enthusiastic Electronics Engineering Intern to gain hands-on experience designing, building, testing, and debugging electronic hardware. Working alongside senior engineers, you’ll contribute across the development cycle—from schematic and PCB design through prototyping, testing, debugging, and documentation.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities and Duties&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build, assemble, test, and debug prototype circuits and PCB assemblies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Assist with schematic capture and PCB design.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Use lab equipment such as oscilloscopes, multimeters, power supplies, and signal generators for testing and troubleshooting.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support soldering, rework, and other hands-on laboratory activities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and test firmware for microcontrollers and embedded systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Analyse test results and document designs, tests, and project progress.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with senior engineers to troubleshoot technical issues and improve hardware performance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Follow engineering and laboratory safety procedures.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Qualifications and Skills&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Currently pursuing a Master’s degree in Electrical/Electronics Engineering or a related field.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Understanding of analog and digital circuit design.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with PCB design tools such as Altium, KiCad, or Eagle.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on experience with electronics lab equipment and basic soldering.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Programming experience in C, C++, Python, or similar.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with STM32, ESP32, Arduino, or other microcontrollers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Knowledge of communication protocols such as I²C, SPI, UART, CAN, or USB is a plus.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong problem-solving, communication, and teamwork skills.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on experience through university, robotics, or personal electronics projects is highly valued.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;EU citizenship required.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Benefits&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Flexible working hours&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Generous holiday allowance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Car parking&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Enhanced maternity &amp;amp; paternity leave&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Mental health and wellbeing support&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Auterion&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are building the leading software platform for AI-powered autonomous systems for enterprise and government customers. Our team is supporting the most important missions and solving the most challenging problems.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Auterion, we bring together the sharpest minds who love to solve the hardest problems. Join a vibrant team built on innovation, openness, and excellence, where you’ll be empowered to develop ideas, collaborate across all levels, and make an impact that matters.&lt;/p&gt;<p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.ch">Jobs in Switzerland</a> on Arbeitnow</a>

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Nebius:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Nebius is leading a new era in cloud infrastructure for the global AI economy. We are building a full-stack AI cloud platform that supports developers and enterprises from data and model training through to production deployment, without the cost and complexity of building large in-house AI/ML infrastructure.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Built by engineers, for engineers. From large-scale GPU orchestration to inference optimization, we own the hard problems across compute, storage, networking and applied AI.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Listed on Nasdaq (NBIS) and headquartered in Amsterdam, we have a global footprint with R&amp;amp;D hubs across Europe, the UK, North America and Israel. Our team of 1,500+ includes hundreds of engineers with deep expertise across hardware, software and AI R&amp;amp;D.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;The Product&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In a rapidly evolving world, trust in AI depends on AI agents being grounded in fresh, verified real-world data. Search is the foundation that makes this possible. We are building an agent-native search platform designed specifically for AI systems rather than human users. Our product provides programmatic, low-latency, and observable search APIs that AI agents use to retrieve, filter, and reason over real-world information at scale.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;The Role&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;We are looking for a Senior Software Engineer to build the rendering infrastructure behind a novel search engine designed for agentic AI. In this role, you will design systems that transform modern web applications into high&amp;nbsp;quality structured content for search and AI. You will work on browser rendering, JavaScript execution, and large-scale rendering infrastructure capable of processing billions of pages efficiently. Modern websites increasingly rely on client-side rendering, dynamic data loading, and complex application frameworks. Your work will ensure we can reliably render, understand, and extract valuable information while minimising cost &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;and latency.&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;In this position, your responsibility will be to:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design and build large-scale rendering systems for modern web applications&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop browser-based rendering infrastructure capable of executing complex JavaScript applications reliably&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Research how modern frontend frameworks render and deliver content&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Improve rendering quality, completeness, and performance across diverse websites&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Optimise rendering cost, latency, resource utilisation, and throughput at internet scale&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Translate rendering research into reliable production systems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You may be a good fit if you:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Have 5+ years of experience as a software engineer working on production backend or&amp;nbsp;infrastructure systems and are an expert in several of the following areas:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Browser Rendering&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Chromium rendering pipeline — DOM, Layout, Paint, and Compositing&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;JavaScript execution inside browsers and rendering lifecycle and page readiness&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Headless browser execution and browser instrumentation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Chrome DevTools Protocol (CDP)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Playwright, Puppeteer, Selenium, or similar frameworks Modern Web Applications&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;React, Vue, Angular, Svelte, and modern frontend architectures&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Server-side rendering (SSR), client-side rendering (CSR), and streaming rendering&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Single-page applications (SPA) and Progressive Web Apps (PWA)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Resource loading, lazy loading, and modern JavaScript bundles&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Strong candidates may also have experience with:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Building and operating high-throughput content processing pipelines at internet scale&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Distributed systems design and performance optimisation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Open-source contributions or active involvement in the engineering community&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Conference talks or technical publications&lt;/li&gt;
